I saw Rodney announce that death, and I pitied you.  I performed the
invocation a few minutes after you, and entered the planes 20 minutes
or so after you (stupid lawful mysterious force), but at least lawfuls
find archons and titans much friendlier.

First of all, you should know that you had a bit of bad luck.  More
often than not, there are no titans or archons on the plane of air.
Next time you'll be way overprepared, and they won't be there.  C'est
la vie.

but that brings me to my next point:  for a 1st ascension, I'd be a
bit more prepared.  polypile yourself up a ring of conflict.  own a
scroll of scare monster (won't help with archons, but would help with
most other nasties).  Have a +7 silver saber wielded in the 2nd hand
at basic proficiency.  Have a charged wand of death ready to take out
the titan.  Alchemize yourself some blessed potions of full healing
for more hitpoints.  (and may as well get yourself some blessed gain
ability while you're at it).  Train your spell of magic missile so you
can cast it at 0% failure.  At XL21, a spell of magic missile can do
more damage than +7 Stormy even with GoP.  You don't need to be next
to the titan to hit it with magic missile, and about 3 hits with lvl
21 magic missile can take down a titan.  Archons are more troublesome;
without a rubber chicken handy, I don't know how to deal with them
other than hack em up with two-weaponed +7 weapons.

Personally, I prefer a different source of reflection so I can wear
the "oLS, but I'm not sure this has ever proven useful.  Anyway, you
can go with SDSM, CoMR, intrinsic invisibility, and the "oLS if you
want.  If I'm lawful or neutral, I usually have SDSM and get my MR
from another quest artifact.  I think most would feel that your GDSM
and "oR should be enough, though.

Anyway, I think conflict would have been a big help for you:  the
damage monsters do to each other is nice, but the damage that the
monsters aren't doing to you when they attack others is very nice.

Lastly, avoid the clouds on the plane of air; getting paralyzed on
that plane is bad.

As you probably know, Elbereth and scrolls of earth don't do diddly on
the plane of air, but they might help in a similar situation on the
plane of fire.

